  "id": "COMPOUND:280 - PROTEIN:4928",
  "verbalization": "Bleomycin is implicated in the regulation of T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that bleomycin acts as a target for multiple compounds, including palmarumycin CP18 and 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn target CD3. This indicates a potential pathway where bleomycin may influence CD3 through these intermediates, possibly by modulating the activity of the compounds they interact with. The shared involvement of palmarumycin CP18 in targeting CD3 across different targets (LB2241-RCC, MCF-10A, and COLO-792) suggests a possible functional relationship between these compounds and CD3, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the interaction network, where bleomycin may serve as a bridge or regulator in the broader context of cellular signaling involving CD3.",
